{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Therefore you shall send gifts</b> — gifts, as in 'gifts for his daughter.' The meaning: give yet more gifts to the Philistines, as was your custom; perhaps they will help you." "<b>Moreshet-Gat</b> — a city in the land of the Philistines." "<b>The houses of Akhziv</b> — Yefet said: a city. In my opinion: the alef is added, and it is like 'and it was in Khziv'; perhaps it belonged to Judah and they could not help Israel in the time of its trouble, and the alef of akhziv is added, like akdeḥ, and it is the way of rhetoric to speak thus — as in 'you will be like Deman' and 'you will be like Aroer,' and likewise many."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:38.541901446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}